# `s = "a $(n + 1) b"` - the parenthesised interpolation form.
#
# julia.json promises string_literal = delimiter, repeat(content |
# string_interpolation | escape_sequence), delimiter; and
# string_interpolation = "$" followed by an identifier or a parenthesised
# bracket form. Extents are read off the source text: the literal opens at
# byte 10, the `$(` at 13, and the literal closes after byte 23.
roots 1
mends 0
holds string_literal
holds string_interpolation
spans string_literal 10 24
spans string_interpolation 13 21
